-- GAME ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Title       Abu Simbel Profanation
  Publisher   Dinamic, 1985
  Version     1.0

-- YOU NEED ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Your own copy of the original game, saved beside this patch:

  File        Abu Simbel Profanation (1985)(Dinamic)(ES)[a][a].z80
  MD5         2909c2f0f18eca08479a74ad6dc8d193

  The patch carries none of the game's code. It only works with that exact
  dump, under that name or any other: anything else is refused, with a
  message naming the file it wants.

-- WHAT IT DOES --------------------------------------------------------------
  Moving figures become Next hardware sprites, so they keep their own colours
  and no longer take on the scenery's (colour clash). Game logic is unchanged.

  Colours     Default (the game's own) plus: Enhanced, chosen on the menu, off
              by default.
  Enhanced    The Spec256 conversion's colours on every figure: Johny Jones
              and the temple's creatures in their own colours over the game's
              unchanged rooms; the colour table of the build approved on
              2026-11-03, byte for byte. Source: Enhanced colours: from
              Spectrum Magic's older Spec256 conversion, painter not
              established.

  Pace        original (-1.24% measured in JNext 1.1.104, against the original
              .z80 on a 48K machine, game state in lockstep)

  Changes     1.0: figures as Next sprites; the game's plotter runs whole at
              28 MHz with its screen writes kept off the shown screen, and a
              pace window keeps every plot a little under the original's time,
              so the game is never slower; Sinclair's 48K ROM as the whole alt
              ROM (no dependence on NextZXOS's ROM3, 26.11 included); the
              game's speed restored after every hook; R kept as the
              original's; the Spec256 Enhanced colours approved on 2026-11-03,
              unchanged; the English text set; three tested cheats

  Note        Keys: on the menu hold 3 for the keys or 2 for a Kempston
              joystick (the tune reads its keys between notes; there is no
              option 1, as in the original). In play O left, P right, Q to T a
              low jump, A to G a high jump, CAPS SHIFT+SPACE quits. Every
              figure, Johny Jones and the temple's creatures, is a Next sprite
              in the game's own colours, so the rooms keep theirs; figures
              still sink behind water and ice as in the original. Enhanced
              colours (off by default): the Spec256 conversion's colours on
              the figures. Language: Spanish, as the game is, or English text.
              Known issues: in JNext it runs 0.7-1.7% faster than the original
              by scene; quiet stretches of one room up to 2.1% faster, and one
              attract-mode stretch 0.2% slower. Missing: hardware testing; the
              tape's loading screen; a natural playthrough to the ending; the
              archive's Lives (0-255) cheat (it asks for a number),
              Invulnerability (hangs in water) and Transform yourself (unclear
              in testing).

-- MENU ----------------------------------------------------------------------
   1  Immunity
   2  Infinite lives
   3  No enemies

  The archive's POKEs for this release, each tested alone in the simulator,
  same keys with and without it: Immunity (no deaths), Infinite lives (lives
  never fall), No enemies (the archive's 'Transform objects': the moving
  enemies are neither moved nor drawn). Left out: a second infinite lives (the
  same effect), Lives (0-255) (asks for a number), Invulnerability (hangs in
  water), Transform yourself (more deaths in one test).

